<title>BRAZIL: Brazil suspends controversial food import controls.</title>
<headline>Brazil suspends controversial food import controls.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian Health Ministry has suspended a controversial decree which would have introduced a series of bureaucratic controls on food imports, the government's official gazette said.</p>
<p>Argentina, whose exports to Brazil would have been particularly affected by the measures, complained last week that the decree was contrary to the spirit of the Mercosur customs union to which the two countries belong.</p>
<p>Argentina's ambassador to Brazil Diego Guelar welcomed the quick suspension of the measures and said harmonizing health controls for food imports within Mercosur would be discussed by officials from the group's four member countries.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
